# XBD <wctype.h>
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# Semantic content of <wctype.h> that the generated header check cannot
# express: the types are scalar or integer, and WEOF is the one <wchar.h>
# defines. Each says why it has no mutant yet.

assertion  XBD.wctype.h.001
anchor     basedefs/wctype.h.html#DESCRIPTION/wctrans_t
anchor     basedefs/wctype.h.html#DESCRIPTION/wctype_t
class      required
since      2001
says       <wctype.h> alone defines wctype_t and wctrans_t as scalar types (a
           value can be cast from zero and tested) and wint_t, as described for
           <wchar.h>, as an integer type.
test       t/001-scalar-types.c
nomutant   compile-time check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants

assertion  XBD.wctype.h.002
anchor     basedefs/wctype.h.html#DESCRIPTION/WEOF
class      required
since      2001
says       <wctype.h> alone defines WEOF, a constant expression of type wint_t,
           with the same value as the WEOF of <wchar.h>.
test       t/002-weof.c
nomutant   compile-time check; needs the Tier 0 header mutants
